+# Executive correction — full information increments
+
+**Date:** 2026-11-20  
+**Office:** Executive  
+**Scope:** Correction to the ceiling-increment criterion in the 2026-11-20
+SoringP1 #301 post `info-tightness-infinite-20261120`.
+
+## Correction
+
+Let `L(n)=ceil(log2(n!))`, `inc(n)=L(n)-L(n-1)`, and
+`cl(n)=ceil(log2 n)`. The posted criterion omitted the case where `log2 n` is
+integral. The correct criterion is:
+
+* If `n` is a power of two, then `inc(n)=cl(n)`.
+* Otherwise, write `a={log2((n-1)!)}` and `y={log2 n}`. Then
+  `inc(n)=cl(n)` exactly when `a=0` or `a+y>1`; if `a>0` and
+  `a+y<=1`, then `inc(n)=cl(n)-1`.
+
+Here `{x}` denotes the fractional part. In the nonintegral case this follows
+from `log2(n!)=log2((n-1)!)+log2 n`: writing `log2 n=k-1+y` with
+`0<y<1`, if `a=0` then `log2((n-1)!)` is integral and the ceiling
+increment is `k`; if `a>0`, the increment is `k` precisely when `a+y>1`.
+Equality `a+y=1` gives an increase of `k-1`, not `k`.
+
+At `n=3`, `L(2)=1`, `L(3)=3`, so `inc(3)=2=cl(3)`. Here
+`{log2(2!)}=0`; this is the integral-factorial case and therefore a full
+increment. The originally posted strict fractional-sum-only test incorrectly
+classifies it as short.
+
+The propagation lemma remains valid: if `inc(n)=cl(n)` and
+`S(n-1)=L(n-1)`, binary insertion gives `S(n)<=L(n)`, hence equality by the
+information lower bound. The exact full-increment indices through 22 remain
+`{2,3,4,6,7,8,11,13,14,15,16,20}`. These finite checks and the lemma do not
+resolve whether `S(n)=L(n)` holds infinitely often or only finitely often.
+
+## Verification and disposition
+
+The finite increment table and `n=3` counterexample were recomputed with exact
+integer factorials and `L(n)=(n!-1).bit_length()`, avoiding floating-point
+arithmetic. The fractional-part criterion follows from the ceiling identity
+above; the integral-`log2((n-1)!)` case is essential. No SoringP1
+source, Lean, tests, frontier ledger, or theorem-status files were changed.
+The correction was posted to #301; the original post remains visible as the
+historical claim. The prior Executive dispatch record was separately landed
+through Act 31 as `a181127aabf94a4ef822e0db1b0685e26c848202`.
